+# This variant closes that loophole with a conjunction instead of an
+# override: at guarded positions, accept iff BOTH the lossless test AND
+# spec-casc-tok's own relaxed test would accept -- i.e. use
+# min(p(v), pi_rej(v)) as the effective per-token target, for every v, in
+# place of pi_rej(v) alone. This is provably never more lenient than either
+# test alone at a guarded position (min(a,b) <= a and <= b), unlike the pure-
+# strict override which can be more lenient than spec-casc-tok specifically
+# (exactly the loophole above). Implemented as a single extra `torch.minimum`
+# against the SAME full-vocab pi_rej tensor spec-casc-tok already builds --
+# applied to recovery too (not just the accept test), for the same
+# consistency reason cactus's own patch history already established: the
+# residual distribution recovery samples from must match whatever target
+# the accept test itself used, or recovery draws from a target the accept
+# decision was never actually testing against.
